  "concept": "certificate-rejection-message",
  "description": "Each shell decides a sync failure was a TLS certificate rejection by matching rustls' 'invalid peer certificate' Display prefix, then shows sync.errors.certificateNotTrusted. The marker is a third-party string: a rustls reword reverts all three shells to the generic URL/password message. Two tests catch a reword against a real handshake — tls::tests (a_privately_signed_server_is_rejected_without_its_root) and the Android instrumentation PlatformTrustTest; the TypeScript, Swift and JVM unit tests feed in hand-written copies and cannot. Belongs in Rust as a typed SyncError variant (AGENTS.md 'Where logic lives' 1) — see the Gap in docs/spec/sync.md.",
  "lockStatus": "unlocked",
